  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Niger: Justice for Stability in Niger: Strengthening Niger&#x2019;s Judicial Capacity to Counter Violent Extremism and Transnational Organized Crime (JSN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Judicial and security sector institutions and personnel involved in counterterrorism and TOC cases, including judges, prosecutors, clerks, and investigators from the Ministry of Justice, the Specialized Judicial Unit for Counterterrorism and TOC, the Central Service for the Fight against Terrorism and TOC, and the Niamey Court of Appeal.Indirect beneficiaries: Victims and alleged perpetrators of terrorist acts, and community members.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reinforce Niger&#x2019;s justice sector capacity to counter violent extremism, terrorism, and transnational organized crime (TOC) while upholding human rights standards.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve skills and tools for judicial and security actors to handle TOC and terrorism-related cases, including from a gender perspective.</narrative>
  </description>
